diag(pip): Read the main set with the same probes as the lens, in the same frames

The lens image improved from about 8/255 to 34/255 with the exposure fix and its sky now matches
the main view, so the remaining darkness is not an exposure problem. Three candidates have been
ruled out with evidence rather than by argument:

 - the lens shader's own grade: scope_lense_brightness/contrast/saturation/gamma are all 1.0 in the
   player's user.ltx, so grade_second_vp is skipped entirely;
 - the name keyed remap: every G-buffer target of the second set is created through createUnique
   (r4_rendertarget.cpp), so $user$albedo, $user$accum and friends do resolve to the lens set;
 - the accumulator contents: the lens accumulator probes bright (134/2/127) while the lens combined
   image is dark, so the lighting ran.

What is left needs one comparison the current probes cannot make, because they only read the lens
set: the same numbers for the MAIN set, in the same frame. A lens render whose rt_Accum is weaker
than the main's points at the lighting or the combine; one whose rt_Accum matches and whose
generic0 does not points at the post process tail, which the lens never runs while the reference
build did (its SVP frame ran phase_pp and only skipped blur, bloom, SSR and water, and its lens
texture was copied from the swapchain - i.e. the post processed frame). Both possibilities are
named in the code and the probe throttle is now shared by the two passes so the numbers line up.